Horizontal privilege :  escalation occurs when an attacker can access resources or data belonging to other users with the same level of access. 
For example, a user might be able to access another user’s account by changing the user ID in the URL.

Vertical privilege  : escalation occurs when an attacker can access resources or data belonging to users with higher access levels.
For example, a regular user can access administrative functions by manipulating a hidden form field or URL parameter.

